    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d96">

                <pb facs="0095" n="75" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg75"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Dayton</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 533.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-04-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 21, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I thank you for your interesting despatch
                    of the 4th of April, No. 446. The time which was limited for the execution of
                    the convention for removing <pb facs="0096" n="76" xml:id="pg76"/> the French
                    government tobacco will expire on the 23d. I give you a copy of a
                        correspondence<anchor n="*" xml:id="d96-f1"/> that has arisen with regard to
                    an extension of the time.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * *</p>
                <p>This suspension is made for that reason, and for that only.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William L. Dayton</hi> Esq.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d96-f1" n="*" xml:id="d96-f1-content">
                <p>[See correspondence with the French legation.]</p>
